.Dd 2026-06-04
.Dt NOMAD-RECONCILE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nomad-reconcile
.Nd re-sync the catalog to the current data root
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm nomad reconcile
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm nomad reconcile
re-synchronizes the catalog with the files under the active
.Sy NOMAD_DATA_ROOT .
The catalog
.Pq MySQL
lives on this Mac's internal disk and stays there even after the data root
changes, so after adopting or reverting a drive the catalog must be brought
back in line with whatever files are actually present.
It takes no arguments and is idempotent.
.Pp
The command performs the following steps:
.Bl -enum -width Ds
.It
Brings the content stack up against the current data root
.Pq Ic docker compose up -d .
.It
Waits for the admin service to be reachable.
.It
Triggers a Workshop
.Pq STL
rescan, which adds catalog rows for files now present and removes rows for
files that are gone.
The rescan runs only after the admin service is up against the correct data
root, so it never prunes the catalog against a stale or unmounted library.
.It
Runs the Kiwix self-heal pass so the Information Library reloads any ZIM files
the current data root carries
.Pq see Xr nomad-fix-kiwix 1 .
.El
.Pp
.Nm nomad reconcile
does not change which services are marked installed: the admin service derives
that from the live container list on its own, so reconcile leaves it alone.
It runs automatically as the final step of
.Xr nomad-adopt-drive 1
and when a drive is ejected and the previous library is restored; run it by
hand if the catalog ever looks out of step with the files on the active data
root.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic nomad reconcile
Re-sync the catalog to the files under the active data root.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nomad 1 ,
.Xr nomad-adopt-drive 1 ,
.Xr nomad-fix-kiwix 1 ,
.Xr nomad-stl 1
